# The endpoint takes a thousand legs and the decoder read as many as the body
# carried, so a body of 5,500 was walked in full to be told the count: 373 MB
# across four hundred requests, against 188 MB once the walk stops at the bound.

title: the decoder reads past the legs the endpoint takes
file: internal/ledgerhttp/decode.go
run: go test -count=1 -run TestTheLegsPastTheBoundAreNotRead -v ./internal/ledgerhttp/
--- before
	read := len(items)
	if most, ok := counted[leaf(path)]; ok && read > most {
		read = most
	}
--- after
	read := len(items)
